110	    /**
111	     * The maximum size for a transaction ID in bytes when serialized as UTF-8. This value is used to determine
112	     * whether the transaction ID provided in
113	     * {@link FDBDatabase#openContext(Map, FDBStoreTimer, FDBDatabase.WeakReadSemantics, FDBTransactionPriority, String)}
114	     * should be truncated or dropped. Note that Java {@link String}s are encoded using UTF-16, so using
115	     * {@link String#length()} is insufficient to know if the transaction ID will be too large if it contains
116	     * any non-ASCII characters (though it is recommended that all transaction IDs be printable ASCII characters
117	     * as those are the ones that render well in the logs). To get the size in UTF-8, one can serialize the
118	     * string to UTF-8 using {@link String#getBytes(Charset)} or check its encoded size using
119	     * {@link Utf8#encodedLength(CharSequence)} or an equivalent function.
120	     *
121	     * <p>
122	     * Note that this limit is inherited by the Record Layer from the FoundationDB client. In particular, the
123	     * {@link com.apple.foundationdb.TransactionOptions#setDebugTransactionIdentifier(String)} method will
124	     * not accept IDs longer than 100 bytes in length.
125	     * </p>
